From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Reset pre-cost API requests during fresh costing.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later.

UI dependency: apply msi-executeaction-ui-selection-transfer.patch too.
Windows v15-2/3 now measures the fresh UI handoff. It reconstructs selection
properties before execute costing, so this request reset can remain unchanged.
Do not use this reset alone for FULL/REDUCED installs. Native final strict,
L0, paired local i686 L2 and cross-review are still gates before clean-g6.

Windows v14 seq950 API requests are accepted and visible immediately, but
none survives the following CostFinalize. Clear fresh requests before
processing the explicit selection properties; do not change maintenance.

This prevents normalized pre-cost Local requests from becoming unintended
ADDLOCAL seeds. The unchanged api/none variant pairs assert all before,
after and published states. Shared v14 conformance, RULE_API.

--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -2338,6 +2338,15 @@
     /* read components states from the registry */
     ACTION_GetComponentInstallStates(package);
     ACTION_GetFeatureInstallStates(package);
+
+    /* Windows v14: pre-cost API requests do not seed fresh costing. */
+    if (!msi_get_property_int( package->db, L"Installed", 0 ))
+    {
+        MSIFEATURE *feature;
+
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( feature, &package->features, MSIFEATURE, entry )
+            feature->Action = feature->ActionRequest = INSTALLSTATE_UNKNOWN;
+    }
 
     if (!process_overrides( package, msi_get_property_int( package->db, L"INSTALLLEVEL", 1 ) ))
     {
